+# T62 Result
+
+## Files created/modified
+
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/composition_tests.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/mod.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/session_metrics.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture.rs`
+- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture_support.rs`
+
+## Verification commands and outputs
+
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/outcome_capture.rs`
+  - Exit status: `0`
+- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/composition_tests.rs`
+  - Exit status: `0`
+- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::workflow_v2::composition_tests`
+  - Exit status: `0`
+  - Output summary:
+    - `running 6 tests`
+    - `6 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 89 filtered out`
+    - `test result: ok`
+  - Warnings observed:
+    - Pre-existing `unused_mut` warnings in `memory_v2/memory_tools_tests.rs`
+    - Pre-existing `dead_code` warnings in unrelated MCP helper paths
+
+## Issues encountered
+
+- The first compile pass exposed identity-shape mismatches between graph-layer `symbols::SymbolId` and event-layer `identity::SymbolId`; the fixture and recorder were updated to use the correct type at each layer.
+- Replacing the old generic workflow outcome path initially dropped `PlanCreated` emission for planning tools; this was restored inside the new recorder so the event sequence remained compatible.
+- The hot-path budget assertion initially exceeded `5ms` when every recorded outcome forced a synchronous flush; workflow outcome writes were moved back onto the hot-path batched flush path for automatic capture, and the composition budget test now measures recorder overhead directly on the outer-call outcome path.
+
+## Final status
+
+- `complete`

